    "text": "UIIII KALENDAS MAI, NATALE SANCTI GEORGII MARTYRIS.\nGEDWOLMEN AWRITON GEDWYLD ON HEORA BOCVM BE \u00f0AM halgan were \u00f0e is gehaten\nNu wille we eow secgan \u00fe\u00e6t so\u00f0 is be \u00f0am, \u00fe\u00e6t heora gedwyld ne derige digellice \u00e6nigum.\nSe halga georius w\u00e6s on h\u00e6\u00feenum dagum rice ealdorman under \u00f0am re\u00fean casere \u00fee w\u00e6s Datianus\n\u00dea het Datianus \u00f0a h\u00e6\u00f0enan gegaderian to his deofolgildum his Drihtne on teonan, and mid manegum\n\u00dea geseah se halga wer \u00fe\u00e6ra h\u00e6\u00f0enra gedwyld hu hi \u00f0am deoflum ons\u00e6gdon and heora Drihten\n\u00deine godas, casere, syndon gyldene and sylfrene, st\u00e6nene and treowene, getreowleasera manna\nHw\u00e6t \u00fea Datianus deofollice geyrsode ongean \u00f0one halgan wer, and het hine secgan of hwilcere byrig\n\u00dea andwyrde Georius \u00f0am arleasan and cw\u00e6\u00f0, Ic eom so\u00f0lice Cristen and ic Criste \u00feeowige.\nGeorius ic eom gehaten, and ic h\u00e6bbe ealdordom on minum earde, \u00f0e is gehaten Cappadocia, and me\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Datianus, \u00feu dwelast, Geori, geneal\u00e6c nu \u00e6rest and geoffra \u00feine lac \u00feam unoferswi\u00f0endum\nGeorius \u00fea befran \u00feone feondlican casere, hw\u00e6\u00f0er is to lufigenne, o\u00f0\u00f0e hwam lac to offrigenne, \u00f0am\nHw\u00e6t \u00f0a Datianus mid deofollicum graman het \u00f0one halgan wer on hencgene ah\u00e6bban, and mid\nHet hine \u00fea si\u00f0\u00f0an of \u00f0\u00e6re ceastre al\u00e6dan and mid swinglum \u00fereagen and mid sealte gnidan; ac se\n\u00dea het se casere hine on cwearterne don, and het geaxian ofer eall sumne \u00e6lt\u00e6wne dry.\n\u00dea geaxode \u00fe\u00e6t Athanasius se dry, and com to \u00f0am casere, and hine caflice befran, hwi hete \u00f0u me\nDatianus andwyrde Athanasie \u00f0us, Miht \u00feu adw\u00e6scan \u00fe\u00e6ra Cristenra drycr\u00e6ft?\n\u00dea andwyrde se dry Datiane \u00f0us, Hat cuman to me \u00feone Cristenan mann, and beo ic scyldig gif ic his\n\u00dea f\u00e6gnode Datianus \u00fe\u00e6t he funde swylcne dry, and het of cwearterne l\u00e6dan \u00f0one godes cempan, and\nGeorius \u00f0a beheold \u00feone h\u00e6\u00f0enan dry, and cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t he gesawe Cristes gife on him.\nAthanasius \u00f0a ardlice genam \u00e6nne mycelne bollan mid bealuwe afylled, and deoflum bet\u00e6hte \u00f0one\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 eft se dry, Git ic do an \u00feincg, and gif him \u00fe\u00e6t ne dera\u00f0, Ic buge to Criste.\nHe genam \u00f0a ane cuppan mid cwealmberum drence, and clypode swy\u00f0e to sweartum deoflum, and to\n\u00d0a geseah se dry \u00fe\u00e6t he him derian ne mihte, and feol to his fotum fulluhtes biddende; and se halga\nHw\u00e6t \u00f0a Datianus deoflice wear\u00f0 gram, and het geniman \u00feone dry \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6r gelyfde on God, and l\u00e6dan\nEft on \u00feam o\u00ferum d\u00e6ge het se arleasa casere gebindan Georium on anum bradum hweowle, and twa\n\u00dea geb\u00e6d Georius hine bealdlice to Gode, Deus in adiutorium meum intende; domine, ad adiuuandum\n\u00dea tyrndon \u00fea h\u00e6\u00f0enan hetelice \u00fe\u00e6t hweowl, ac hit sona tob\u00e6rst and beah to eor\u00f0an, and se halga wer\nDatianus \u00fea dreorig wear\u00f0 on mode, and swor \u00f0urh \u00f0a sunnan, and \u00f0urh ealle his godas, \u00fe\u00e6t he mid\n\u00d0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 se eadiga Georius him to, \u00feine \u00f0eowracan synd hwilwendlice, ac ic ne forhtige for \u00f0inum\n\u00dea het se casere his cwelleras feccan \u00e6nne \u00e6rene hwer, and hine ealne afyllan mid weallendum leade,\n\u00dea ahof se halga to heofonum his eagan, his Drihten biddende and bealdlice cwe\u00f0ende, Ic gange into\nAnd he bletsode \u00fe\u00e6t lead and l\u00e6g him onuppan, and \u00fe\u00e6t lead wear\u00f0 acolod \u00feurh Godes mihte, and\n\u00d0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 se casere to \u00feam Cristes \u00feegene, Nast \u00feu, la Geori, \u00fe\u00e6t ure Godas swinca\u00f0 mid \u00fee, and git hi\nNu l\u00e6re ic \u00f0e swa swa leofne sunu, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0u \u00fe\u00e6ra cristenra lare forl\u00e6te mid ealle, and to minum r\u00e6de\n\u00dea se halga martyr mid \u00f0am halgan gaste afylled, smearcode mid mu\u00f0e and to \u00f0am manfullan cw\u00e6\u00f0,\n\u00c6fter \u00f0isum bebead se ablenda Datianus \u00fe\u00e6t mann his deadan godas deorwur\u00f0lice fr\u00e6tewode, and\nHw\u00e6t \u00f0a Georius to eor\u00f0an abeah \u00feus biddende his Drihten gebigedum cneowum, Gehyr nu, God\n\u00c6fter \u00f0isum gebede b\u00e6rst ut of heofonum swy\u00f0e f\u00e6rlic fyr, and forbernde \u00fe\u00e6t templ, and ealle \u00f0a\nEac swylce \u00fea sacerdas suncon for\u00f0 mid, and sume \u00f0a h\u00e6\u00f0enan \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6r gehende stodon; and Georius\nHu magon hi ahreddan \u00f0e fram frecednyssum, \u00feonne hi ne mihton hi sylfe ahreddan?\nHw\u00e6t \u00f0a Datianus gedihte \u00feisne cwyde, and het \u00f0us acwellan \u00feone Godes cempan, Nima\u00f0 \u00feisne\n\u00dea tugon \u00fea h\u00e6\u00f0enan \u00feone halgan wer swa Datianus him gediht h\u00e6fde, o\u00f0\u00fe\u00e6t hi comon to \u00f0\u00e6re\nHe \u00feancode \u00f0a Gode eallra his godnyssa, \u00fe\u00e6t he hine gescylde wi\u00f0 \u00feone swicolan deofol, and him\nHe geb\u00e6d eac swylce for eall Cristen folc, and \u00fe\u00e6t God forgeafe \u00fe\u00e6re eor\u00f0an renas, for \u00fean \u00f0e se\n\u00c6fter \u00f0isum geb\u00e6de he bletsode hine sylfne, and b\u00e6d his slagan \u00fe\u00e6t he hine sloge.\nMid \u00feam \u00f0e he acweald w\u00e6s, \u00f0a comon \u00feyder sona his agene landleode geleofede on God, and\n\u00dea asende Drihten renscuras, and \u00fea eor\u00f0an gew\u00e6terode \u00fee \u00e6r w\u00e6s forburnen, swa swa Georius b\u00e6d\nHw\u00e6t \u00f0a Datianus wear\u00f0 f\u00e6rlice ofslagen mid heofonlicum fyre, and his geferan samod, \u00fea \u00f0a he",
